&lt;p&gt;  &lt;strong&gt; B. Nationally Covered Indications&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt; N&sol;A&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;  &lt;strong&gt; C. Nationally Non-Covered Indications&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; Effective for claims with dates of service on and after December 23, 2009, the Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) determines that the evidence is adequate to conclude that OIVIT does not improve health outcomes in Medicare beneficiaries. Therefore, CMS determines that OIVIT is not reasonable and necessary for any indication under section 1862(a)(1)(A) of the Social Security Act. Services comprising an Outpatient Intravenous Insulin Therapy regimen are nationally non-covered under Medicare when furnished pursuant to an OIVIT regimen (see subsection A. above).&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt; D. Other&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; Individual components of OIVIT may have medical uses in conventional treatment regimens for diabetes and other conditions. Coverage for such other uses may be determined by other local or national Medicare determinations, and do not pertain to OIVIT. For example, see Pub. 100-03, NCD Manual, Section &lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=222&amp;ncdver=2&amp;DocID=40.2&amp;kq=true&amp;SearchType=Advanced&amp;bc=EAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;40.2&lt;&sol;a&gt;, Home Blood Glucose Monitors, Section &lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=92&amp;ncdver=1&amp;DocID=40.3&amp;kq=true&amp;SearchType=Advanced&amp;bc=EAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;40.3&lt;&sol;a&gt;, Closed-loop Blood Glucose Control Devices (CBGCD), Section &lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=98&amp;ncdver=2&amp;DocID=190.20&amp;kq=true&amp;SearchType=Advanced&amp;bc=EAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;190.20&lt;&sol;a&gt;, Blood Glucose Testing, and Section &lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;medicare-coverage-database&sol;details&sol;ncd-details.aspx?NCDId=223&amp;ncdver=2&amp;DocID=280.14&amp;kq=true&amp;bc=gAAAAAgAAAAA&amp;&quot;&gt;280.14&lt;&sol;a&gt;, Infusion Pumps, as well as Pub. 100-04, &lt;a href=&quot;https:&sol;&sol;www.cms.gov&sol;Regulations-and-Guidance&sol;Guidance&sol;Manuals&sol;Internet-Only-Manuals-IOMs-Items&sol;CMS018912&quot;&gt;Claims Processing Manual&lt;&sol;a&gt;, Chapter 18, Section 90, Diabetics Screening.&lt;&sol;p&gt;

&lt;p&gt; &lt;strong&gt;        (This NCD last reviewed December 2009.)&lt;&sol;strong&gt;&lt;&sol;p&gt;

